## 6. Logging Strategy Analysis

### Weak Logging (Typical AI Output)

```python
logger.error("Something went wrong: %s", e)
```

### Strong Logging (Human Reasoning)

```python
logger.error(
    "Request failed | method=%s | url=%s | error=%s",
    method, url, str(e)
)
```

### Key Differences

| Aspect       | Weak Logging | Strong Logging |
| ------------ | ------------ | -------------- |
| Context      | None         | Detailed       |
| Debugging    | Difficult    | Easier         |
| Traceability | Low          | High           |
| Usefulness   | Limited      | High           |

---

## 7. AI vs Human Logging Comparison

### AI-Generated Example

```python
except Exception as e:
    logger.error("An error occurred: %s", e)
```

### Human-Improved Example

```python
except requests.exceptions.Timeout as e:
    logger.error(
        "Timeout while connecting to %s after 5 seconds",
        url
    )
```

### Comparison

| Feature              | AI       | Human  |
| -------------------- | -------- | ------ |
| Specificity          | Low      | High   |
| Context awareness    | Limited  | Strong |
| Debug usefulness     | Moderate | High   |
| Error classification | Weak     | Strong |

